{"repositoryId":471117197,"availability":"available","full":"nasa/fmdtools","name":"fmdtools","description":"System Resilience Modelling, Simulation, and Assessment in Python","category":"Developer tools","language":"HTML","stars":60,"forks":19,"created":"2022-03-17T19:34:03Z","updated":"2026-10-16T21:40:52Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://nasa.github.io/fmdtools/","topics":["fault-model","hazard-assessment","reliability","resilience","safety","simulation"],"demo":"https://nasa.github.io/fmdtools/examples/Examples.html","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T11:02:38.778Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T11:02:38.778Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T11:02:38.778Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-17T11:02:38.778Z","stars":60,"forks":19}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["fmdtools (Fault Model Design tools) is a Python library for modelling, simulating, and analyzing the resilience of complex systems. With fmdtools, you can (1) represent system structure and behavior in a model, (2) simulate the dynamic effects of hazardous scenarios on the system, and (3) analyze the results of simulations to understand and improve system resilience.","The fmdtools library provides the computational support needed to perform a simulation-based analysis of systems resilience, as shown above. This analysis of resilience can enable the quantification of risk and safety of given hazards in complex systems where there are dynamic interactions between the system, operators, and the environment."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nasa/fmdtools/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"8479041593265267d002ac92cb9e62fe26fff9c9dfde1b070f5ad5673acb5b42","extractedAt":"2026-10-17T11:02:38.916Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T11:02:38.916Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"fmdtools (Fault Model Design tools) is a Python library for modelling, simulating, and analyzing the resilience of complex syst